# MoPhongMayTrenTau — PUBLIC_REFERENCE maritime training simulators

This workspace develops a **training-only** collection of marine-instrument UI simulators. The target is to reproduce the operation sequences of a specific hardware model/controller/firmware, **not** to provide navigation, depth measurement or real-ship decision support.

## Current status (FCV-588 public-reference V31, 2026-10-16; QA HOLD)

- **FURUNO FCV-588**: interactive offline original-art classroom simulator,
  profile `F1-public-reference-20`, scenario v7, settings schema18. It
  supports physical keys/TrackPad/hold and direct pointer-drag rotary input,
  LF/HF/DUAL/Zoom,
  source-gated synthetic sonar/alarms/NAV, protected IEC/NMEA settings,
  deterministic replay and **seven instructor D15 lessons**. V31 repairs
  option-dependent transaction revocation and Alarm notices, resets BRILL's
  inactivity deadline on adjustment, and adds compact Range/Gain/BRILL/MODE
  current/pending LCD feedback. V30 nested configuration presentation remains;
  V29 FUNC and V28 face/LCD corrections are preserved. OEM
  user-interface/firmware/transducer and hardware-operation fidelity
  remain **unapproved**. Current 64 operator functions + separate D15:
  60 operator synthetic subsets, 3 partial (C11/D09/D14), 1 not implemented
  (D04), plus the separate synthetic D15 platform.
  D09 is held by default unless an instructor explicitly declares an
  **optional synthetic Tankenmaru fixture**, never hardware entitlement.
  At phone widths the **training-only** face reflows to preserve a readable
  LCD and at least 44px touch controls, explicitly **not OEM bezel geometry**.
  Every public-release claim remains **HOLD**.
  V30-B/E are repaired with scoped state/native-browser evidence. Integrated
  acceptance remains OPEN: latest targeted Node52/53 has an incorrect Auto
  fixture expecting Manual preset text, and required counsel/full regression
  have not completed. The failing fixture is preserved, not silently repaired.
  White Line remains Off/On; percentage/Edge is not implemented without a source contract.
- **MDC-2060, FAR-2127, AIS R5, NS4000**: profiles are held for later independent validation; no working UI is claimed.
- **KODEN J2000**: model identification is unresolved, status `HOLD`.
- No third-party packages, hardware drivers, serial, NMEA transmitters, network publishers, live AIS or real equipment are used by the simulator.

## Start locally

Requires Node.js 22 or newer. From `C:\Work\MoPhongMayTrenTau`:

```powershell
npm run check
npm start
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:4173`. The local server only listens on loopback. For offline training only.
V31 actual scoped verification: state/compatibility42/42 PASS; the later
control/transaction Node run **52 PASS /1 FAIL**, not GREEN. Native operator
Chrome passed **284/284** checks on1366×768,1920×1080,360×800,390×844, each with
132 actual SHA-verified response bodies over33 paths. All12 current screenshots
were opened. Full Node/Python and the older full/FUNC/config/LCD Chrome suites
have **not** been rerun on V31; historical V30 numbers are not current proof.
Do not treat this source as a release candidate or a completed QA checkpoint.

The normal settings decoder is strict profile20. A separate validated
profile19 committed-settings importer preserves schema18 and original startup
storage bytes; a saved Tankenmaru preference never grants virtual hardware.
Original profile19 replays reject under profile20 rather than silently migrate.
The unchanged White Line setting remains Off/On. All50 criteria and22 Tasks
are assessed; acceptance stays14/50 and6/22, all65 public claims HOLD.

